            "Yes, because conducting a high-explosive aerial fireworks display is an abnormally dangerous activity imposing strict liability for resulting physical damage.",
            "Yes, under the doctrine of res ipsa loquitur, because fireworks do not detonate prematurely in the absence of negligence."
